WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:14.920
Big 5's Trap
Duel Monsters Quest

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.060
I bet you never imagined that you'd see me again.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:32.300
I know that you teamed up with Pegasus to take over Kaiba Corporation.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.240
That's right!  It's your fault that we were...

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.270
I'll never forgive your actions.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.320
I use my authority as president to fire you immediately!

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.760
Wait a second!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.190
You're acting pathetic!

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:01.230
It all began when you lost against Yugi Muto.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.400
What?

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:08.560
Mr. Seto, we teamed up with Pegasus in order to regain the public's trust in our company.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.620
That's right.  We did it for the company.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:18.350
As proof, we even developed a new adventure game based on Duel Monsters.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.690
Adventure game?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.660
President, let's play a game with our jobs on the line.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.130
If you clear the game, we lose.

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:33.080
But if you don't clear it, we're not fired.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.130
I see.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.000
You're issuing a challenge.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:39.370
Fine.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:40.570
Big brother?

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:45.180
When challenged to a game, Seto Kaiba doesn't run away.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:48.610
Big brother!

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.160
Big brother, why did you agree?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.800
This is a trap!

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.800
I know that.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.030
Then why?

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.300
Even if I force them out, they'll think of a plan for revenge.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:16.540
I'll crush them completely and show them my strength!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.060
Insert your cards into the deck case.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.880
The canopy will close.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.200
Please remain seated.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:52.350
Canopy locked.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.350
The game will begin.  Standby.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.450
Big brother, this is too dangerous alone.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.800
Don't be afraid.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.120
Start it up, Mokuba.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.550
Big brother...

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.990
I promise to win!

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:13.930
Big brother!

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.600
Big brother...

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:00.540
You think this simple game can defeat me?

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.970
Come out, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.340
Burst Scream of Destruction!

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:19.760
Blue-Eyes!

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:25.900
What?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.840
Dragon Capture Jar?

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.300
Blue-Eyes!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.390
Big brother!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.660
Big brother!

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.600
Big brother!  Wake up!

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:04.460
His consciousness has been turned into data and trapped inside the game.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.710
Say what?

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:11.940
Unless he clears the game, Seto's consciousness will be stuck in the virtual world forever.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:15.020
Kaiba Corporation now belongs to us.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.280
Exactly.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:20.220
Mokuba, we'll imprison you too.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.770
Big brother...

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.310
Where's Mokuba?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.800
Damn!  That's...

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.040
He got away!

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.620
Mokuba has escaped.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.130
You fools!  Find him immediately!

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.670
Don't get flustered.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.160
Mokuba will definitely return.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.060
What?

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:05.230
Such a brave younger brother would never leave Seto behind.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.170
But you don't know for sure.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.770
And no matter who arrives, this game is impossible to clear.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:17.920
Look!  I have new cards in stock!

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.950
Let me see!

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.590
Yugi...

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.450
Mokuba?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.300
Kaiba is trapped inside an adventure game world?

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.240
And if you lose, you can never leave?

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.300
That's no game!

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:43.160
Yugi, please save my big brother.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:49.750
But since Kaiba Corporation's executives are involved, this will be difficult.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:58.620
My big brother's dream is to build Kaiba Lands around the world to make children happy.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.110
That's really Kaiba's dream?

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.040
It's true.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:08.360
That's why he devoted his whole life to Kaiba Corporation.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.500
He never had time to relax.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.860
Don't worry, Mokuba.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.080
We didn't say that we wouldn't help.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:22.880
Yeah!  We know how strong your bond is with Kaiba!

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.280
Yugi...

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.660
We're going, Grandpa!

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.840
Be careful!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:29.640
Yeah!

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.250
I'm going too!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:37.630
When did you grow so strong, Yugi?

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:42.360
The Big Five has taken control of Kaiba Corporation.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.100
What should we do?

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:49.200
I heard them say that Kaiba Land's simulator has the same program.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.220
There it is.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.600
It's functional!  We can access it!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.480
One, two, three...

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.280
Only three of us can go.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.680
Me, Yugi and-

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.040
The last one is...

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.000
I'm going.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.230
Mokuba?

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.600
If you lose the game, you can never come back!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:33.000
There's no point living in a world without my big brother!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.030
Mokuba...

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.340
That settles it.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.520
Honda, you stay behind.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.300
Promise that you'll come back.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.960
Don't worry.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.780
I promise that we'll return.  With Kaiba.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.400
Honda, do it.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.030
All right!  Here it goes!

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.720
I believe in you.

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.680
They've left.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.740
He really came back.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:15.360
Mokuba brought Yugi Muto.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:22.520
Saruwatari, go to Kaiba Land and trap Yugi Muto and Mokuba inside the game world.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:29.840
I wonder if this world has a connection with Duel Monsters.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:36.370
We don't know the rules of this world, so we need to be careful.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.480
I know.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:41.710
Where are we?

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.940
I don't think we can pass through here scot-free.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:49.510
I've seen this place before.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.930
It's a ghost!

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.520
Clown Zombie, Armored Zombie and Dragon Zombie?

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.660
They're Duel Monsters.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.040
In that case...

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.430
How do I do this?

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:33.770
Go, Rude Kaiser!

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.640
Come out, Dark Magician!

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.210
Attack!

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.120
You just have to tell them to attack?

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:01.330
Give up already!

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.760
Go, Flame Swordsman!

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.440
Flaming Battle Sword!

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:17.200
Oh no!  Stop your attack, Jonouchi!

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:29.860
Flame Swordsman!

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:33.530
A Zombie gains attack points every time it resurrects.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:35.460
They're immortal.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:41.470
Jonouchi, remember your battle against  Kotsuzuka at Duelist Kingdom.

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:45.340
You know how to defeat Zombies.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.510
Oh yeah!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.950
Zombies have 0 defense points.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:54.640
I activate Shield & Sword!

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:04.090
All right!  Now's your chance!

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.760
Go, Dark Magician!

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.430
Black Magic!

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.970
We did it!

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:20.620
There's a picture of gold coins.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.840
It's this world's money.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.780
I didn't regain my life points!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.660
I see.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.140
This represents our life.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:31.620
Damn!  What happens if it reaches 0?

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:37.420
A fairy?

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:43.180
In video games, fairies give hints.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.240
Hey, wait!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.450
Huh?

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.440
I lost sight of it.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.940
What is it, Mokuba?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.600
It's a town.

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:12.950
This is what they eat?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.100
Jonouchi!

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.210
It's a super rare card!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.070
I'm buying it!

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.220
You can't.  Look at the price.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.140
2000 gold?

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:31.750
I got this card when I defeated the monster.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:33.250
Only five?

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:34.700
I can't afford it.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.630
Let's hurry up and find my big brother instead.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:38.320
Yeah.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.860
Okay, let's split up and gather information.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.340
Did you learn anything?

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:05.120
Not at all.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.310
I learned a lot of stuff.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:13.980
This morning, someone transporting a person inside a cage went to Owess Temple.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.680
Could it be Kaiba?

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:16.860
Probably!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:20.960
In order to get to Owess Temple, we have to cross this desert.

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:23.160
Easier said than done.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.560
Mokuba!

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.720
This is impossible!

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.400
Let's go back, Mokuba!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:40.620
Be quiet!  I have to find my big brother.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:43.940
What's that?

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.820
A tornado!

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:55.870
Yugi, are you okay?

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:56.840
Yugi?

00:15:58.660 --> 00:15:59.640
Where are we?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.730
We were blown back to the town.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:07.880
Mokuba.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:13.580
Do you wish to cross the desert?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.820
Old man, do you know how?

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:21.370
You need a Niwatori card to cross the desert.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.330
Niwatori?

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.320
This card!

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.760
Old man, how can we acquire that card?

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:32.700
You need a Niwatori card to cross the desert.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.370
We heard you the first time.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:39.310
You need a Niwatori card to cross the desert.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.110
His dialogue repeats.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:45.310
So we can't leave this town without a Niwatori card.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.000
Let's split up again and find the Niwatori card.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.560
It must be here somewhere!

00:16:57.060 --> 00:17:02.460
Yugi Muto, we won't let you rescue Seto Kaiba.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.680
A lot of time has passed already.

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:07.220
Stay patient.

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:11.760
Yugi may be a gaming genius, but he can't clear the game that quickly.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.710
You're right, but...

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:18.220
I know!  To pass the time, I'll tell you a special story!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:22.380
The title is "Hiroto Honda's First Love During Middle School."

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.730
I definitely don't want to hear this story.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.090
Really?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:31.990
How about my elementary school graduation speech about wanting to become a pilot?

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:36.910
Do you seriously not realize the danger we're in?

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:44.300
It seems we have enemies in this world too.

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:48.040
Anzu, let's lock the door and build a barricade.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:49.580
Okay.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.890
It's no good.  I can't find one anywhere.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.910
I went to all the shops in town.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:59.080
Maybe this game has a bug.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.280
Let's search again.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.320
What is it, Yugi?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.740
I found it!

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:08.600
What?

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:14.370
"Want to risk your life and challenge the champion?"

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:17.970
"The winning prize is a Niwatori card."

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:20.830
"We're waiting for you to try."

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.120
" - Manager of the Shadow Coliseum"

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.850
All right!  We found it!

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.350
What?  You want to challenge the champion?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.800
Oh my, such brave youngsters.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:43.730
The champion is so strong that we were having trouble finding challengers.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:50.620
It's decided!  We'll begin the match immediately!

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:53.110
Wear this mask and cape.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:57.720
Is it really that dangerous?

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:02.120
All you have to do is battle until your life points reach 0.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.780
Until they reach 0?

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:04.780
I'll enter.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.450
Jonouchi!

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:12.080
If your life points reach 0, there's no guarantee that you can leave this world.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.390
In that case, since you've already lost life points...

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.170
Don't be dumb!

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:20.740
It doesn't matter if I'm here or not.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:24.120
But without you, we'll never clear this game.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:24.840
But...

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.640
Jonouchi.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:30.780
Anyway, I've decided that I'm entering.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:41.290
Ladies and gentlemen, we've finally found a challenger to face our invincible champion.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:47.230
To protect his two brothers, this terrifying pig fights back against the wolf.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.280
Live, pig!

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.760
Die, wolf!

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:54.060
It's Joe the Wolf Killer!

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:56.320
I'm betting on the challenger!

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.970
You idiot!  The champion won't lose!

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:02.570
I'm getting a bad feeling.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.010
You can do it, Jonouchi!

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:12.680
Your opponent will be the invincible champion Butterfly!

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:18.280
The champion is a girl?

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:35.370
The female warrior opposing Yugi's team at the coliseum is Mai Kujaku!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:41.120
Thanks to Mai's help, Yugi crosses the desert and reaches Owess Temple.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:45.360
Kaiba isn't there, but a girl that looks like Mokuba is.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.960
What?  Yugi is the legendary hero?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:54.230
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
DM Quest 2
Yugi the Legendary Hero

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.160
Duel, standby!

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:08.210
The flask glistens

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:16.060
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:25.040
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:32.810
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:38.640
Shower of happiness

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:42.760
I will shower you with it

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:51.030
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:55.270
Shower of happiness

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:59.390
You are not alone

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:06.110
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
